fbcon: draw the boot logo even when the console is quiet

The appliance boots with `quiet loglevel=3` (silent boot, see
docs/PLAN.md), but fbcon refuses to draw the built-in boot logo
whenever console_loglevel <= CONSOLE_LOGLEVEL_QUIET (4). That gate
exists so desktop distros don't flash penguins over their quiet
boots - here it defeats the whole point of the Boompi kernel logo
(linux-splash.fragment + kernel-logo.ppm), which fills the dark
window between firmware handoff and boompi-ui.

Drop the loglevel check. Kernel *text* stays suppressed by
loglevel=3; only the logo bitmap is drawn at fbcon takeover.

--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c
@@ -1006,9 +1006,6 @@
 
 	info = fbcon_info_from_console(vc->vc_num);
 
-	if (logo_shown < 0 && console_loglevel <= CONSOLE_LOGLEVEL_QUIET)
-		logo_shown = FBCON_LOGO_DONTSHOW;
-
 	if (vc != svc || logo_shown == FBCON_LOGO_DONTSHOW ||
 	    (info->fix.type == FB_TYPE_TEXT))
 		logo = 0;
